Replacements for common Windows fonts, generated the same way as in
Valve's Proton: Liberation Sans, Serif and Mono renamed to Arial, Times
New Roman, Georgia and Courier New, and Microsoft Sans Serif and Nirmala
UI merged from Noto Sans fonts. These fonts are not the Microsoft fonts;
the names are used for compatibility with programs that require them.

proton-openbsd(1) links them into wine prefixes, where Proton's wine
expects them in C:\windows\Fonts. Proton's CJK fonts (from Source Han
Sans and Ume) are not included.
